o the system in May (meaning it was actually paid within April, not delayed!). \"a contabilidade tirou o resumo com ele 'em aberto' porque eu lancei o PIX no sistema só em maio\" — the resumo shows 0 for... hmm which line? The summary says \"April pró-labore (R$ 3,200) was actually paid on 2026-04-30 (posting lag).\" The resumo shows a pró-labore 3,200 line in 2026-04 (April accrual = 3,200). Was \"March accrual = 0\" related to April payment being missing... hmm no.\n\nLet me re-read the resumo: 2026-03 row: pró-labore = 0. 2026-04 row: pró-labore = 3,200. Client statement: the April pró-labore (accrual basis April, R$ 3,200) was paid on 30/04 but the resumo listed it as \"em aberto\" — meaning the resumo lists April accrual as unpaid (pró-labore 3,200 might be the accrued value, and March 0 might mean something else). Whatever — what matters: R$ 3,200 of PL was actually paid on 30/04/2026 → cash within the window.\n\nSo what about March/2026? The 2026-03 line shows pró-labore = 0. If accrual basis March was 0, there's nothing to pay in March (unless a prior accrual was paid late, but all prior months were paid within the month per the resumo... the resumo doesn't show payment status except where it shows 0). Actually the resumo columns are probably accrual-based amounts, and March 0 means no March PL accrual. In that case cash-basis PL for the window (payments May/2025 → April/2026):\n- Accruals May/2025..Feb/2026: 10 × 3,200 = 32,000 paid within the month (pattern).\n- Accrual March 2026: 0 → nothing.\n- Accrual April 2026: 3,200 paid on 30/04/2026 ✓.\nTotal cash-basis PL = 35,200.\n\nWait — but why was March accrual 0? Maybe the company skipped March PL, or maybe \"April\" payment was booked as \"March\" in the system... The client says \"pró-labore de abril ... foi pago em 30 de abril\" (April pró-labore was paid on April 30). No mystery about March. The only residual unknown is: does the 2026-03 pró-labore = 0 mean no accrual (in which case, 35,200 is final), 